Article 3 (Formulation of Comprehensive Development Plans, etc.)
(1) Where the Mayor of a Metropolitan City, the Governor of a Do, or the Governor of a Special Self-Governing Province having jurisdiction over a remote island on the outskirts of the national territory (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor or Do Governor") intends to prepare a draft development plan for an island under their jurisdiction (hereinafter referred to as a "draft Si/Do development plan") pursuant to Article 5 (4) of the Act, the Mayor or Governor may hear the opinions of the relevant Mayor or head of a Gun having jurisdiction over the island.
(2) A draft Si/Do development plan prepared under paragraph (1) shall contain the following:
1. The matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 5 (2) of the Act;
2. An outline of projects to be promoted in connection with the matters under subparagraph 1 (including project scale, implementation period, and expected effects), and investment plans.
(3) The term "where minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree are to be amended" in the proviso to Article 5 (7) of the Act means any of the following:
1. Changing the area or project cost of an individual project included in the comprehensive development plan under Article 5 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "comprehensive development plan") by not more than 10 percent;
2. Changing the name of an individual project included in the comprehensive development plan;
3. Reflecting in the comprehensive development plan any amendment to, or abolition of, a major infrastructure project plan confirmed under another statute or regulation, after that project plan has been incorporated into the comprehensive development plan.
